  --------------------------------------------------------------------
  parameter-shift          32       1.8       4.8        6.6      45.5
  QLTO                      4     490.4       3.7      494.1      41.6
  -> QLTO classical overhead is 74.81x MORE EXPENSIVE than parameter-shift

  ===== Heisenberg N=4 | M=16 | G=3 =====
  method             circuits     build    decode  CLASSICAL     (run)
  --------------------------------------------------------------------
  parameter-shift          96       5.5      12.1       17.7     145.4
  QLTO                      4     509.5       2.7      512.2     140.0
  -> QLTO classical overhead is 29.01x MORE EXPENSIVE than parameter-shift

  If QLTO is cheaper here too, the circuit-count claim stands unqualified.
  If it is more expensive, the claim needs the crossover stated: the saved
  quantum time has to exceed the extra local CPU time.
